= Programming with Rudiments using the listener class =

The [../classes/html/classlistener.html listener class] provides methods for monitoring multiple file descriptors for activity.

Servers commonly need to listen on multiple sockets for client connections.  They can listen on multiple inet sockets, multiple unix sockets, or a combination.  Technically, they could listen on any set of file descriptors, whether they are all sockets or not.  The listener class can be used to make this possible.

The following example creates both an inet socket server and a unix socket server, adds them to a listener, and waits for activity on either socket.  When a socket becomes ready, the program checks which one it is and reports accordingly.

